# Two players, level 1, and **the second one does the rescuing.**
#
# `movies/level1-rescue.zmv` walks Zeke into the cheerleader five times and so
# takes `victim_claim_a` — collision id 5, the branch that latches the id
# *itself* into the victim's `$18`. Nothing has ever taken id 6, the branch
# three bytes away that latches `$8000` instead, because it needs the *other*
# player to arrive first. That one word is the whole of "bit 15 names the
# player" on a victim, and `score_add`'s `BMI` is what reads it, so this movie
# is also the only thing that credits `score_slot_1` for a rescue rather than
# for a kill.
#
# So: Zeke stands still and Julie walks up-left into the victim. The order
# matters and it is the only thing this movie has to get right — the latch at
# `$83:A364` means whichever player touches her first settles her fate, and
# a second claim after that is `victim_latched` (which is a different untaken
# site, and also on the list — see the tail of this file).
#
# The boot prefix through frame 1484 is level1-2p.zmv's, unchanged, including
# controller 2 joining on the "PLAYER LEFT / PLAYER RIGHT" screen.
#
# Retune by watching where it actually gets to:
#   zamn_headless <rom> shot.png 4200 -m movies\level1-2p-rescue.zmv --at 1900,2000,2100
