# Gameplay. Julie goes up and left into the cheerleader; Zeke does not move at
# all until she has her, so there is no doubt about who arrived first. The
# score going 0 -> 1000 with the credit landing in the *second* slot is the
# thing to watch.
2:1860   Up+Left
2:2100   Up
2:2220   Left
2:2340   -

# With the rescue settled, both players move as a pair — identical inputs on
# the two ports from here on — and head for the cluster of victims in the
# north-west of the map (the level lists three inside a 200x200 box up there:
# $9F:84FB entries at 175,430 / 184,282 / 355,492). Moving together is the
# point: `actor_overlap_pass` reads the *outer* record's collision id once and
# then walks every record below it, so a victim that is the outer record of a
# pass with both players inside its box has its handler called twice in the one
# pass — and the second call is `victim_latched`, the branch that proves the
# latch guard does anything at all. Whether the victim sorts as the outer
# record is a property of the depth sort rather than of the input, so this is
# an attempt rather than a guarantee; the coverage report says which way it
# went.
#
# Y is held throughout (the fire button, not B — see level1-2p.zmv). B is not
# nothing, though: it cycles weapons, which porting $80:EA63 turned up. See
# docs/analysis-tools.md.
